{"chapter": "stacks-properties", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04YA", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-properties-lemma-quasi-compact-space}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:588a618100f1233262dd78fa5196fc713c0cd4e3cb12b19057a2e13abd2a80f8", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe following definition is equivalent with the definition for algebraic\nspaces by\nProperties of Spaces, Lemma <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:120004a001d2068b080142ca13b5dde5db47811f79bbe4463a56f43889b1bafa", "unit_id": "tag:04YA:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "stacks-properties", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "04YA", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0003": "$|\\mathcal{X}|$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-quasi-compact}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:086b218376c2256e72d0bf662883ce927920be3259d3f5b50e6eedd6163817ab", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4b9c69fbeb5d5d1ffb8fbfb8ee86305d46c05b90c84892fe9b0b6b0f4d005c92", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an algebraic stack.\nWe say <MATH_0002> is <TEXTITOPEN_0001>quasi-compact<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\nif and only if <MATH_0003> is quasi-compact.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7bf001c5fe8c985be135b30f66150eb699f213f7452159027bddfc25828b8755", "unit_id": "tag:04YB:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-properties", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04YA", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0003": "$U \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0004": "$U$", "MATH_0005": "$U \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0006": "$U$", "MATH_0007": "$U \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0008": "$U$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{U} \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{U}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\item", "STRUCT_0007": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-quasi-compact-stack}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:dda1782c94b1668c02c2bd076ae5b8a4b1ba413a64c70af4e4850577c184db5e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:debfdde2f1b9c48e81f5b8c8c2e41c6b7360eade159cdb35e730a640afb6c390", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an algebraic stack.\nThe following are equivalent:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0002> is quasi-compact,\n<STRUCT_0003> there exists a surjective smooth morphism <MATH_0003>\nwith <MATH_0004> an affine scheme,\n<STRUCT_0004> there exists a surjective smooth morphism <MATH_0005>\nwith <MATH_0006> a quasi-compact scheme,\n<STRUCT_0005> there exists a surjective smooth morphism <MATH_0007>\nwith <MATH_0008> a quasi-compact algebraic space, and\n<STRUCT_0006> there exists a surjective morphism <MATH_0009>\nof algebraic stacks such that <MATH_0010> is quasi-compact.\n<STRUCT_0007>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:883920b4c2e6d2ec3da18e3ca7dfedb82d52473faadb6363fd3d3f8cccfe507e", "unit_id": "tag:04YC:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-properties", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04YA", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{U}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{U} \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0003": "$|\\mathcal{U}| \\to |\\mathcal{X}|$", "MATH_0004": "$|\\mathcal{X}|$", "MATH_0005": "$\\Rightarrow$", "MATH_0006": "$\\Rightarrow$", "MATH_0007": "$\\Rightarrow$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0009": "$|\\mathcal{X}|$", "MATH_0010": "$U$", "MATH_0011": "$U \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0012": "$|U| \\to |\\mathcal{X}|$", "MATH_0013": "$U' \\subset U$", "MATH_0014": "$|U'| \\to |X|$", "MATH_0015": "$U' = U_1 \\cup \\ldots \\cup U_n$", "MATH_0016": "$U_1 \\amalg \\ldots \\amalg U_n \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-characterize-surjective}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-disjoint-union-affines}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:87fd25a8351ad9d9a20fecb6d27af140f24cb6bb016a960a3474a91b0aa0ba57", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1bf5fd0390a8c95f96e1d252ea158f669407b66402375ac3895a4edf70463358", "source_text": "We will use\nLemma <REF_0001>.\nSuppose <MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002> are as in (5).\nThen since <MATH_0003> is surjective and\ncontinuous we conclude that <MATH_0004> is quasi-compact.\nThus (5) implies (1). The implications\n(2) <MATH_0005> (3) <MATH_0006> (4) <MATH_0007> (5)\nare immediate. Assume (1), i.e., <MATH_0008> is quasi-compact, i.e., that\n<MATH_0009> is quasi-compact. Choose a scheme <MATH_0010> and a surjective\nsmooth morphism <MATH_0011>. Then since <MATH_0012>\nis open we see that there exists a quasi-compact open <MATH_0013>\nsuch that <MATH_0014> is surjective (and still smooth).\nChoose a finite affine open covering <MATH_0015>.\nThen <MATH_0016>\nis a surjective smooth morphism whose source is an\naffine scheme (Schemes, Lemma <REF_0002>).\nHence (2) holds.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3877a0e47f2211bc4e721a2c2f6567a6989065c9f043493f14d7465b73afc068", "unit_id": "tag:04YC:proof"}
